### Problem
`STARTUP()` is not timing guaranteed. For example,
```cpp
class Test {
public:
    Test(uint8_t val = 0) {
        DiagPrintf("User App Constructor: %d\n", val);
    }
    ~Test() = default;
};

Test testInstance1(1);

STARTUP(
    DiagPrintf("STARTUP() 1\n");
);

STARTUP(
    DiagPrintf("STARTUP() 2\n");
);

Test testInstance2(2);
```
The output:
```
[+   2][253802946] User App Constructor: 1
[+   3][253802949] STARTUP() 1
[+   1][253802950] STARTUP() 2
[+   1][253802951] User App Constructor: 2
```
### Solution
Introduce a new API `PRE_STARTUP()`, which is executed in previous to the `STARTUP()` and is timing guaranteed.

### Example App
```cpp
void PRE_STARTUP() {
    Serial2.begin(115200);
    Serial2.println("PRE_STARTUP called");
}

void setup() {
}

void loop() {
}
```

