### Problem

VIN on TrackerM hardware on `5.3.0`/`develop` is broken again. 

The power source also always shows as `VIN` when on USB power. 
This is due to `HAL_PLATFORM_POWER_WORKAROUND_USB_HOST_VIN_SOURCE` define. `HAL_USB_Get_State()` is not implemented / always returns `HAL_USB_STATE_NONE`. This forces the `VIN` source even if the PMIC reports USB source due to the following:
```
    switch (powerSourceFromStatus(status)) {
      case POWER_SOURCE_USB_HOST: {
#if HAL_PLATFORM_POWER_WORKAROUND_USB_HOST_VIN_SOURCE
        if (vin || usb_state < HAL_USB_STATE_POWERED) { // <------ This is always true, so SRC is always set to `POWER_SOURCE_VIN`
#else
        if (vin) {
#endif // HAL_PLATFORM_POWER_WORKAROUND_USB_HOST_VIN_SOURCE
          src = POWER_SOURCE_VIN;
          applyVinConfig();
        }
    ...
```

### Solution

Fix the shared interrupt config version to match latest in HAL.
Remove `HAL_PLATFORM_POWER_WORKAROUND_USB_HOST_VIN_SOURCE` from RTL platform 

