## Enable setting of common wifi country codes from ISO 3166-1 alpha-2

### Problem

With the P2 previously we only supported setting the wifi country code to "US". 

### Solution

This PR allows setting some common country codes, along with our best understanding of the MCU-supported channel plan configuration to match these regions. 

### Steps to Test

Set country code to one of the supported versions. Verify that you're able to connect to a corresponding wifi access point in that region. 

### Example App

```c

SYSTEM_THREAD(ENABLED);
SYSTEM_MODE(SEMI_AUTOMATIC);
SerialLogHandler logHandler(115200, LOG_LEVEL_INFO);

static void validate_country_code(wlan_country_code_t input) {
    wlan_set_country_code(input, nullptr);
    wlan_country_code_t cc_type = wlan_get_country_code(nullptr);
    if (cc_type != input) {
        Log.error("expected: %04x got: %04x",input, cc_type);
    }
}

void setup() {
    wlan_country_code_t cc_type = wlan_get_country_code(nullptr);
    Log.info("initial country code: '%c%c'", (char)(cc_type >> 8), char(cc_type & 0xFF));

    validate_country_code(wlan_country_code_t::WLAN_CC_MX);
    validate_country_code(wlan_country_code_t::WLAN_CC_JP);
    validate_country_code(wlan_country_code_t::WLAN_CC_AU);
    validate_country_code(wlan_country_code_t::WLAN_CC_KR);
    validate_country_code(wlan_country_code_t::WLAN_CC_CA);
    validate_country_code(wlan_country_code_t::WLAN_CC_EU);
}

void loop() {
    if (!Particle.connected()) {
        Log.info("Particle connect...");
        delay(3000);
        Particle.connect();
        waitFor(Particle.connected, 30000);
        if (!Particle.connected()) {
            Log.error("Could not connect!");
            return;
        }
  }
    
}
```

