### Problem

When testing Device OS in automated scenarios, we frequently need to recover devices under test from some blocked state caused by, for example, the network registration process.

### Solution

Allow resetting the device and cancelling the cloud connection directly in the USB HAL's ISR.

### Steps to Test

Using [this](https://github.com/particle-iot/particle-usb/tree/reset_req/ch57751) branch of particle-usb:
```js
const usb = require('particle-usb');

async function run() {
    let dev = null;
    try {
        const devs = await usb.getDevices();
        if (!devs.length) {
            throw new Error('No devices found');
        }
        dev = devs[0];
        await dev.open();
        // This should reset the device immediately
        // await dev.reset({ force: true });
        // This should cause the device to disconnect from the cloud immediately
        // await dev.disconnectFromCloud({ force: true });
    } catch (err) {
        console.error(err.stack);
        process.exit(1);
    } finally {
        if (dev) {
            await dev.close();
        }
    }
}

run();
```

