### Problem

1. We've recently increased maximum current and decreased voltage limit when powered by VIN by default in order to allow Electrons and Borons to function without a battery, as well as fixed a problem with Borons incorrectly detecting when they are powered by VIN vs USB Host See https://github.com/particle-iot/device-os/pull/1846 https://github.com/particle-iot/device-os/pull/1921

2. Applications requiring special PMIC settings cannot reliably set them, because of System Power Manager within DeviceOS. There currently exists a workaround for this, but it's not ideal https://community.particle.io/t/1-3-1-rc-1-change-to-boron-solar-charging-via-vusb-behavior/51987/5?u=avtolstoy

These two problems together prevent certain applications e.g. solar.

### Solution

This PR does a number of things:

We've reverted the changes to the default PMIC settings we use when powered by VIN. These are now again 3.88V min, 900mA max for the PMIC to enter DPM mode and reduce current consumption.

When powered by USB host or USB-compliant adapter, the current limit is automatically negotiated with the other side and voltage input limit is still set to 3.88V.

Another addition is a higher level power configuration API allowing to notify the system about the expected PSU parameters. These settings are persisted and work correctly even without the application running (e.g. while the device is in safe mode). See 'Example App' section for the example usage.

This PR also adds a couple of methods to query current power source, battery state and state of charge more easily. See 'Example App' section as well.

