### Problem

Support for Twilio SIMs by default in system firmware was required: to use a custom port, avoid requiring a custom user app and maintain connectivity in Safe Mode.

### Solution

- Twilio SIM have a sequential range of IMSI (SIM serial number) numbers that can be detected.
- Port 4500 is used for Twilio vs. the default port 5864.
- UDP Server port is set at runtime based on Network Provider.
- Keep alive ping defaults are set at runtime based on Network Provider, although they are currently still 23 minutes for all.  They can always be overridden in a user app with Particle.keepAlive(seconds);
- Tests included

### Steps to Test

