### Bugfixes

- [`[PR #1254]`](https://github.com/spark/firmware/pull/1254) [`[Fixes #1241]`](https://github.com/spark/firmware/issues/1241) `WiFi.connecting()` was returning `false` while DHCP is resolving, will now remain `true`.

This PR changes the polling interval reported for flash/sflash in DFU mode to 0, significantly speeding up DFU programming times.

## Why can we safely set this interval to 0?
1. All flash operations are executed from USB interrupt while processing a specific USB request
2. The host can not initiate a second USB request to the same USB endpoint (DFU uses only endpoint 0) while the previous one is still pending.
3. USB request is responded to only after completing a flash operation.

All this makes an additional delay in `dfu-util` while "waiting" for flash operation to complete or device to change status useless, since the operations complete synchronously. Here is an example from `dfu-util` source code (I've added _NOTE:_ comments in a couple of places):

```c
int dfuse_dnload_chunk(struct dfu_if *dif, unsigned char *data, int size,
		       int transaction)
{
	int bytes_sent;
	struct dfu_status dst;
	int ret;

	// NOTE: Completes synchronously
	ret = dfuse_download(dif, size, size ? data : NULL, transaction);
	if (ret < 0) {
		fprintf(stderr, "Error during download\n");
		return ret;
	}
	bytes_sent = ret;

	do {
		// NOTE: Completes synchronously, state has already been changed
		// to a correct one after dfuse_download had completed
		ret = dfu_get_status(dif->dev_handle, dif->interface, &dst);
		if (ret < 0) {
			fprintf(stderr, "Error during download get_status\n");
			return ret;
		}
		// NOTE: A cursed delay is applied anyway even if the device
		// has already gone into a correct state!
		milli_sleep(dst.bwPollTimeout);
	} while (dst.bState != DFU_STATE_dfuDNLOAD_IDLE &&
		 dst.bState != DFU_STATE_dfuERROR &&
		 dst.bState != DFU_STATE_dfuMANIFEST);

	if (dst.bState == DFU_STATE_dfuMANIFEST)
			printf("Transitioning to dfuMANIFEST state\n");

	if (dst.bStatus != DFU_STATUS_OK) {
		printf(" failed!\n");
		printf("state(%u) = %s, status(%u) = %s\n", dst.bState,
		       dfu_state_to_string(dst.bState), dst.bStatus,
		       dfu_status_to_string(dst.bStatus));
		return -1;
	}
	return bytes_sent;
}
```

