Opening a WICED network connection in one thread while a second thread was paused in the middle of memory allocation would lead to a deadlock of the system, with interrupts off.

The symptoms are a solid cyan LED and user code not running.

This PR patches WICED to remove the deadlock possibility in sys_sem_new.

Program to reproduce the issue. Before the fix the blue LED doesn't blink showing a deadlock. After the fix the blue LED blinks quickly.

```
#include "application.h"

Thread allocatorThread;

void allocatorFn() {
  for(;;) {
    void *ptr = malloc(100);
    free(ptr);
  }
}

void setup() {
  pinMode(D7, OUTPUT);
  allocatorThread = Thread("allocator", allocatorFn);
}

void loop() {
  static bool state = false;
  digitalWrite(D7, state);
  state = !state;
  WiFi.resolve("www.particle.io");
}
```

The new unit test deadlocks with the previous WICED library and completes with the patched WICED library.

