Most of the features of this PR are automatic and happen in the background:
- Power_Management_Handler is called any time USB power source is
  changed or if battery charge falls below 10% (about 3.6V).
- Event is not serviced immediately, but rather in the main thread
  after loop() exits.  This prevents these asynchronous events from
  disrupting code execution.
- With the addition of this EXTI interrupt on PC13, D7 may not be
  used by the user with attachInterrupt() because it's sharing the
  same interrupt with PC13.  Safety code was added for this.
- The default charge rate is set to 500mA.
- Enable INFO_LEVEL debugging to see Battery Voltage and SoC at boot time.
- FuelGauge().clearAlert() was not actually clearing the ALRT flag previously

